# JAVASCRIPT :

- A technology that we use to create websites.
- HTML —> skeleton of website.
- CSS —> changes appearance of website.
- javascript —> provides functionality. (interactive)

**What is JavaScript ?**

- High level(abstraction) { you don’t have to deal with memory management on your device}, interpreted ( program is executed directly, without having to run through a compiler) programming language.
- conforms to the ECMAScript specification
- multi-paradigm. ( you can write your code in many different ways, object-oriented code, functional code etc).
- javascript is the language of the browser.(its the language of the frontend (like browser)).
- it also run on server for more powerful things like, interacting with databases etc. —> that is done by using javascript run-time called Node.js.
- runs on the client/browser as well as on the server.(Node.js)
- giving instructions to a computer.
- the computer follows our instructions.
- instruction we give to computer —> code.
- when computer follows instructions —> code running.
- JS is case - senstive.

**WHY LEARN JAVASCRIPT?**

- its the programming language of browser.
- python, php, C# , Java —> all server side languages.
- build very interactive user interfaces with frameworks like **React , Angular , vue.js.**
- used in building very fast server side and full stack applications. (Node.js)
- used in mobile development (React Native, NativeScript, Ionic).
- used in desktop application development (Electron JS).
- **Syntax :** rules that we have to follow when using a programming language.

**( Order of Operations ) Operator Precedence :** 

- * and / are done first. (same priority) —> so, it’ll calculate from left to right.
- + - are done after. (same priority) —> so, it’ll calculate from left to right.
- we use a built in function —> **math.round(). for floats yk bta dete hein ke kahaan tk round off krna h etc.**
- strings —> (means) text.
- we can add string.
- ‘some’ + ‘text’ = sometext.
- its called —> **concatenation** (combine strings together)
- if i write   —> typeof 2 —> output = ‘number’
- if i write —> typeof ‘hello’ —> output = ‘string’.
- if i write —> ‘hello’ + 3 —> output = ‘hello3’. (js will convert this into a string).
- its called —> **Type coercion / automatic type conversion.**
- ‘$’ + 20.95 + 7.99 =⇒ ‘$20.957.99’
- ‘$2.95’ + 7.99
- ‘$20.957.99’.
- strings also follow **operator precedence**.
- ‘$’ + (20.95 + 7.99).
- ‘$28.9399999999999.8. ( to solve this problem)
- ‘$’ + (2095 + 799) / 100
- ‘$28.94’.
